' Notes — every one cites file:LINE
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
note as N_AUTH #FEE2E2
  **TB1 · the boundary that is not enforced.**
  `auth.py:95-97` `require_user()` returns the single local user and
  its own docstring says //"Never 401s now"//; `main.py:55-56` states
  `/chat` and `/reports*` are deliberately auth-free. That is only safe
  if the ports are private — but `docker-compose.yml:272-273` is
  `"8080:8080"`, which Docker binds to **0.0.0.0**, and so are
  `:86 :133 :171 :202 :351-352`. Every ownership comparison
  (`main.py:343-344`, `main.py:701-709`) therefore compares one
  identity with itself. `docker-compose.yml` declares **no `networks:` block**,
  so every container can reach every other —
  including the four unauthenticated model servers.
  **Flows F1, F4, F5, F6 all cross TB1 unauthenticated.**
end note
N_AUTH .. TB1

note as N_TB2 #FEE2E2
  **TB2 · what crosses, and what mitigates it.** Web pages, pasted URLs,
  cloned GitHub repos, uploaded datasets and CRM free-text all reach the
  model prompt. Mitigations that do exist: content is fenced/delimited and
  the system blocks are folded into one leading message first
  (`llm.py:39-69`); uploaded datasets are **profiled, never executed**
  (`config.py:169`, `core/profile.py`); a dual prompt-injection canary is
  asserted never to reach the assembled prompt
  (`tests/test_dataset_profile.py`). What does **not** exist: any
  instruction-stripping, any provenance tainting of model input, and any
  output-side egress check. Flows F21, F24-F27 all cross TB2.
end note
N_TB2 .. TB2

note as N_OWN #FFFBEB
  **Fall-open authorization.** `main.py:338-341` wraps
  `db.conversation_owner()` in `try/except Exception: conv_owner = None`,
  and `main.py:343` only 404s `if conv_owner is not None`. A SQLite
  error therefore //skips// the check — the comment at `main.py:336-337`
  asserts the opposite. Flow F2 is the affected hop.
end note
N_OWN .. orc

note as N_BODY #FFFBEB
  **Unbounded ingress on F2/F6.** `ChatRequest` (`main.py:184-199`)
  caps neither `messages` nor the base64 `image`/`pdf` strings, and
  `main.py:47-53` installs CORS as the only middleware — Starlette adds
  no default body limit. `LiveGeneration.events` (`main.py:85,97`) also
  retains every token frame for the generation's whole life.
  Unauthenticated + 0.0.0.0 + unbounded = trivial OOM.
end note
N_BODY .. fe

note as N_SQL #FFFBEB
  **F14 is the prompt-injection sink.** `core/sql_guard.py:57-126` is a
  hand-written scanner, not a parser: the checks run on `bare` but the
  string that executes is `cleaned` (`sql_guard.py:156`), and an
  `E'\''` escape-string desynchronises the two — a reproduced bypass
  smuggles `; ATTACH` past both the stacked-statement check
  (`:142`) and the keyword blocklist (`:146`).
  What actually holds the line is `engines/sql.py:124-132`:
  `read_only=True`, `enable_external_access=False`,
  `autoinstall/autoload_known_extensions=False`.
  Separately, `engines/sql.py:201,206` calls DuckDB **synchronously**, inside
  an `async def` — one slow query stalls every user's SSE stream.
end note
N_SQL .. sqle

note as N_NET #FFFBEB
  **TB2 egress, F21.** `core/net.py:103-162` is the only place a
  user-influenced URL is fetched: scheme allowlist (`:94-95`), DNS
  resolved and //every// A record checked before connect (`:82-86`),
  each of ≤3 redirect hops re-validated (`:147`), time and size capped.
  Residual gaps — the validated IP is discarded at `net.py:99` and httpx
  re-resolves at `:137` (**TOCTOU / DNS rebinding**); the size cap at
  `:153-155` runs //after// `resp.content` has buffered the whole body;
  `100.64.0.0/10` (CGNAT / Tailscale) is not blocked; there is no
  total deadline and `socket.getaddrinfo` (`:76`) has no timeout.
end note
N_NET .. ioe

note as N_ARC #FFFBEB
  **F24 · hostile archives.** `core/archive.py` is the strongest module
  in the repo — magic-byte sniffing, never `extractall()`, zip-slip
  checked twice (`:157`, `:223`), symlinks/hardlinks/devices refused
  (`:153-156`, `:251-253`), four bomb caps plus a live streaming budget
  (`:200-208`). Two residual gaps: extraction is **fully synchronous**, called
  from a FastAPI `async def` (`uploads.py:99/103`), so a multi-hundred-MB
  archive runs on the event loop; and the byte budget is **per call**
  (`archive.py:216`), so N concurrent uploads each get 2048 MB.
  `enforce_quota_and_ttl` (`core/repo.py:94-119`) treats
  `<workspace_dir>/uploads` as one entry, so a single TTL expiry
  deletes every conversation's extracted uploads at once.
end note
N_ARC .. upl

note as N_SYNC #FEE2E2
  **TB3 ingress, F17-F20.** The RS256 signing key is written to
  `/data/sf_jwt_key.pem` (`syncworker/secrets.py:50`) — i.e. **the same volume**
  as the warehouse, mounted read-write into the orchestrator
  (`docker-compose.yml:269`) and holds the warehouse the LLM queries.
  The JWT itself carries no `iat`/`nbf` and no skew allowance
  (`sf_auth.py:32-38`).
  A RAG-indexing failure is swallowed at `syncworker/main.py:174-184`
  while the watermark still advances at `:188` — a **permanent index gap**.
  Salesforce deletes are never propagated
  (`syncworker/main.py:147-154`), so F18/F20 leave withdrawn CRM
  records readable forever.
end note
N_SYNC .. sw

note as N_STORE #FFFBEB
  **Data-store hygiene.** `db.connect()` (`db.py:195-205`) re-executes
  16 DDL statements plus a full-table de-dup `DELETE` (`:181-186`) on
  **every** call — 34 call sites (31 × `closing(connect())` in `db.py`,
  plus `auth.py:48`, `health.py:79`, `main.py:36`), and one `POST /chat`
  performs at least six. `uploads`, `url_documents`, `repos` and
  `repo_chunks` carry **no foreign key** (`db.py:84,102,114,123`), so
  `delete_conversation` (`db.py:334-340`) orphans them — and because
  conversation ids are client-supplied (`history.py:92-97`), a
  recreated id **inherits the previous conversation's rows**.
  `auth.py:48` `_oldest_user()` leaks the connection it opens.
  DuckDB per-object tables have no PRIMARY KEY or index
  (`syncworker/storage.py:140`), so every upsert `DELETE … WHERE Id IN`
  is a full scan.
end note
N_STORE .. sqlite

note as N_RPT #FEE2E2
  **F4 · the widest CRM leak.** `core/report_paths.py` correctly rejects
  `..`, separators, absolute paths, dotfiles, NUL and symlink escape
  (`:31-47`), but there is **no extension allowlist and no authentication** —
  `main.py:257-259` and `:262-271` declare no
  `Depends`. `/reports` receives both narrative `.docx`/`.pdf`
  (`engines/report.py:256`) **and** CSV/XLSX exports of raw warehouse
  rows (`engines/sql.py:407-409`), so anyone who can reach :8080 can
  enumerate and download every export any analyst has ever produced.
end note
N_RPT .. rp

